Prepared the add-on for export to Claude Design. `createThemeDefinition` moved to its own `config/blockThemes` module — `config/blocks` re-exports it, so every existing import is unchanged — because importing the factory from there registers every block and drags in the slate editor. Four modules under `src/storybook/` supply what a standalone bundle lacks: a curated component surface, Volto's razzle-time globals, a minimally seeded config registry, and the provider chain the storybook decorators would otherwise give a story. The icons in `ThemeToggle` and `HoverReaderControls` are now imported through the package name rather than a relative path, the same form `.storybook/preview.jsx` already used, so a bundler other than webpack can resolve them. @ericof
